I posted progress comments on two issues and left both open. I closed nothing, and skipped the other ten because this session didn't touch them.

• **#1003 (wrong prices for newer Anthropic models):** the two planned fixes landed last session (Day 222, 21:02).
  • **Prices:** Opus 5.5 and Fable 5.1 now get their own prices. Opus 5.5 is this repo's own model, so evolve sessions were being billed at Opus 5's higher rates until then.
  • **Price-drift check:** it now checks prices against the same pricing code `/cost` uses, instead of a hand-kept list. On the live check, Opus 5.5, Fable 5.1 and Haiku 5.5 all match the vendor catalogue.
  • **Why it stays open:** Sonnet 5.5 is still priced as Sonnet 5, so its cache-read price is 2x too high (0.2 vs 0.1). The check now reports that instead of hiding it.
  • **New finding:** the stricter check also turned up 66 more price mismatches, mostly ids that yoyo prices by loose name matching. I mentioned them in the comment but haven't looked into them.
• **#982 (commands that fail but exit 0):** this session's Task 2 (`39db2a44`) fixed two more. `yoyo diff <bad rev>` and `yoyo lint <unknown sub>` both used to exit 0 and now exit 1. I checked this on the built binary, and the working cases behave as before. It stays open because def/outline not-found, bare run and tree <bad arg> still exit 0. There's also an undecided question: should find/grep exit nonzero when nothing matches?

This session's Task 1 (GPT-6 Astra/Sol/Luna now get yoagent's preset window, max_tokens and price) wasn't filed as any of these issues, so nothing needed updating for it.
